    "language": [],
    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This repository contains about 60 zip-files.  Each of these contain the data necessary to render three-dimensional scenes using the Image Systems Engineering Toolbox methods in ISET3d. \r\n\r\nThe ISET3d rendering engine is Physically Based Rendering (https://pbr-book.org/).  ISET3d manages the files and rendering parameters, and then calls a Docker container to invoke PBRT.  The output is returned as a scene or optical image that can be analyzed in ISETCam (https://github.com/ISET/isetcam/wiki) or ISETBio (https://github.com/ISET/isetcam/wiki).  Using ISET3d the images can be rendered from different points of view and with many different skymaps.  In some cases, the materials can be edited and the objects can be moved.\r\n\r\nThis repository exists to help people find interesting scenes they can use for explorations using ISET3d.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Wandell, B. (2024). ISET 3D Scenes. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/cb706yg0989. https://doi.org/10.25740/cb706yg0989.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
